                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="tab-d27e2351" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-d27e2351-parent">
                           
                           <p><img title="Head Coach Trent Troxell" src="/athletics/images/coach_troxell_trent_22-23.jpg" alt="Head Coach Trent Troxell" width="200" height="215" data-entity-type="" data-entity-uuid=""></p>
                           
                           <p><span style="font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;"><strong>Trent Troxell, Head Coach/Recruiting Coordinator</strong></span><br><span style="font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;"><a href="tel:4054221490">405.422.1490</a></span><br><span style="font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;"><a href="mailto:trent.troxell@redlandscc.edu">Email</a></span></p>
                           
                           <p><span style="font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;">Trent Troxell became the sixth head coach in Redlands Community College baseball history
                                 on June 1, 2024. In his first season, he led the Cougars to their first winning record
                                 in 12 years, finishing 29-25 and closing the year with six wins in the final eight
                                 games, including a victory over 18th-ranked Murray State. He coached four all-conference
                                 players in 2025: Tyson Eastwood (First Team, Gold Glove SS), Nick Smith (First Team
                                 DH), Easton Andrews (DH), and Nate Anderson (Gold Glove CF).</span></p>
                           
                           <p><span style="font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;">Prior to Redlands, Troxell served as an assistant coach at Vernon College, where he
                                 oversaw base running and offensive strategy. During his time there, the team ranked
                                 in the top 30 nationally in stolen bases and top 60 in batting average. He also helped
                                 coach Clark Candiotti, who was selected in the 4th round of the MLB Draft by the San
                                 Diego Padres. Before Vernon, Troxell led baseball operations for the Burkburnett Blacksox
                                 in Texas, where he developed over 200 players who advanced to collegiate programs.
                                 In 2019, the organization was named “Most Improved” and finished second at the Nuch
                                 Tournament in Colorado.</span></p>
                           
                           <p><span style="font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;">As a player, Troxell competed at Dodge City Community College, batting .336 as a sophomore,
                                 before finishing his career at Southwestern Oklahoma State University. At SWOSU, he
                                 was part of the 2016 Great American Conference championship team that earned a spot
                                 in the NCAA Division II Regional Tournament.</span></p>
                           
                           <p><span style="font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;">A 2012 graduate of Fort Cobb-Broxton High School, Troxell earned a bachelor’s degree
                                 in business in 2018. He and his wife, Calli, reside in Yukon, Oklahoma.</span></p>
                           
                           <p>&nbsp;</p>
                           
                           <p><img title="Palmer Stevens Headshot" src="/athletics/images/Palmer_Stevens_Asst.jpg" alt="Palmer Stevens Headshot" width="200" height="205"></p>
                           
                           <p><span style="font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;"><strong>Palmer Stevens, Assistant Coach/Pitching Coach</strong></span><br><span style="font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;"><a href="tel:4054221490">405.422.1490</a></span><br><span style="font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;"><a href="mailto:palmer.stevens@redlandscc.edu">Email</a></span></p>
                           
                           <p><span style="font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;">Palmer Stevens enters his 1st year as an assistant baseball coach at RCC. &nbsp;Palmer
                                 started his playing career at Redlands CC and finished his career at Bethany College,
                                 graduating with a Bachelors in Exercise science. As a player, Palmer logged over a
                                 hundred innings as a starter and had 86 strikeouts. Coach Palmer spent two years at
                                 Central Christian college where he earned his master’s in Strategic Leadership. In
                                 his first two years as the pitching coach he helped lowered the team ERA. and helped
                                 the pitching staff set a school strike out record.</span>&nbsp;</p>
                           
                           <p>&nbsp;</p>
                           
                           <p><img title="Blake McQuain Headshot" src="/athletics/images/Blake_McQuain_Asst.jpg" alt="Blake McQuain Headshot" width="200" height="208"></p>
                           
                           <p><strong><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;">Blake McQuain, Assistant Coach</span></strong></p>
                           
                           <p style="margin: 0in; margin-bottom: .0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;">Blake McQuain is a graduate of Dale High School and played baseball at Redlands Community
                                 College from 2018-2020. In the 2018-2019 season McQuain was on the Region 2 Conference
                                 Runner-up team and graduating from Redlands with his Associates degree.</span></p>
                           
                           <p style="margin: 0in; margin-bottom: .0001pt;">&nbsp;</p>
                           
                           <p style="margin: 0in; margin-bottom: .0001pt; font-variant-caps: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-feature-settings: normal; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-variation-settings: normal;"><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;">After Redlands McQuain finished his playing career at Southeastern Oklahoma State,
                                 where he holds a conference record for hits in a game and was an All-Conference selection.&nbsp;</span><span style="font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;">Blake graduated from Southeastern with a Bachelor's degree in safety and a Masters
                                 degree in Sports Administration.&nbsp;</span><span style="font-family: '.SF UI',serif;"></span></p>
                           
                           <p>&nbsp;</p>
                           </div>
